.TH SINDOOK-CONFIG 1 "2026-08-31" "sindook 0.11.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sindook-config \- inspect and change saved settings
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sindook config list
[\fB\-json\fP]
.br
.B sindook config get
\fIKEY\fP
.br
.B sindook config set
\fIKEY VALUE\fP
.br
.B sindook config unset
\fIKEY\fP
.SH DESCRIPTION
Inspects and changes Sindook's managed configuration: the same public
data the \fBinit\fP and \fBcontacts\fP commands maintain, exposed for
setup scripts and dotfiles. The configuration never contains private
keys or passphrases.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B default-identity
the identity used when no \fB\-i\fP is given. \fBset\fP validates that
the file exists and stores its absolute path.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
sindook config get default-identity
sindook config set default-identity ~/keys/work.key
sindook config unset default-identity
sindook config list
sindook config list -json
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sindook (1),
.BR sindook-init (1),
.BR sindook-contacts (1),
.BR sindook-paths (1)
